## Stack
- React + Vite + strict TypeScript + Tailwind CSS.
- Supabase for authentication and database access.
- React Router for routing.
- Reuse installed dependencies; avoid unnecessary packages.

## Context and workflow
- Read docs/requirements.md before feature work.
- Read docs/database-schema.sql before database integration.
- Treat supplied SQL as schema reference; verify deployed schema before relying on it.
- Inspect relevant files only. Work on the requested stage.
- Avoid unrelated refactors, speculative abstractions, and repeated repo scans.
- Ask only when missing information blocks correct implementation.
- Do not silently substitute mock data for failed requests.
- Finish with a concise summary: changes, checks, blockers.

## Architecture
- Organize code by feature: auth, catalog, cart, orders, staff.
- Keep Supabase operations in feature service modules.
- Keep database types separate from domain/UI types.
- Generate database types from the actual schema; never fabricate generated types.
- Validate external inputs and persisted browser data.
- Include loading, empty, error, and retry states where relevant.

## Cart and checkout
- Represent domain money as integer paise; explicitly map database money types.
- Derive cart totals; browser totals are estimates.
- Validate prices, options, availability, quantities, and identity server-side.
- Create orders and items atomically through a trusted operation.
- Enforce checkout idempotency in the backend.
- Preserve the cart on failure; remove submitted items only after confirmed success.

## Quality
- Build accessible, responsive interfaces with keyboard support.
- Use meaningful tests for business logic, authorization, and critical flows.
- Use isolated test data; never run destructive tests against production.
- Run npm run build, npm run lint, and relevant tests after each stage.
- Report unverified security requirements; never claim readiness without evidence.